A||N||14||Haze_Performance||Would anyone like to trade??||||10||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-03-2000||10:06 AM||||Before I go out and buy a decklid I thought I would try to trade someone first.I have a 1985 Silver notchback decklid with luggage rack that I would like to trade for a plain 1985-up NO luggage rack decklid (NO HOLES). I know there are some people out there that like the look of the rack (I not being one of them) For you new members that may not know,  Notchback decklids are all the same size, THE GT lids do not interchange (Unless you change the back of the car) If someone would like to trade or like more info please let me know. You can see some of the car pic's at<BR> <A HREF="http://geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/5773/PHRpics.html" TARGET=_blank>http://geocities.com/MotorCity/Pit/5773/PHRpics.html</A>  <P>Thank's for reading <BR>Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||06-04-2000||10:09 AM||||Come on people...Someone likes the rack...right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||batboy||06-04-2000||02:50 PM||||Nope, I'm doing the same thing. I have a luggage rack on my silver Batmobile too and I'm swapping it for a plain silver one from my dead 87 SE (and probably put a wing on it). Sorry, I can't help you, but it seems like I saw a good plain silver decklid at the boneyard (Westside Auto Salvage) in Emporia, Kansas.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sage||06-04-2000||03:17 PM||||<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dsc_003_1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dsc_004_1.jpg">  <BR>This the stock deck from the car with the rack removed and duraglass used to fill the holes.<BR>You just grind out around the holes (make it concave) so you can get enough filler in there, put tape on the back side so you are not filling a bottomless hole, and finish as you normaly would.  You can do the same thing on the underside if desired.  It's a little more work, but only took a couple hours.  Would be easier if you can find a replacement that is already the right color, but if you are going to have to paint anyway...?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (Sorry about the size of the pics)<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 06-04-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||stimpy||06-04-2000||04:24 PM||||Sage, how did you go about removing the runners? I have a luggage rack on my 86 GT and I am torn between removing it and keeping it as it is an obscure option for the GT. But if I keep it I would at least like to take it off to refinish it. Is it possible to take one off without destroying it?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||06-04-2000||05:08 PM||||Stimpy, I think that luggage rack option is on more Fieros than you think, at least I see them all the time. Anyway, there are at least 5 nuts on the underside of the decklid near the rear that need removed. To get to the rest of the screws, you have to very carefully pop the plastic top off the luggage runners/rails (just the very top, narrow part, not the sides) in order to finish removing it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||06-04-2000||06:28 PM||||I dont know much about the luggage racks... but they are kinda rare on the fastback GT's!  I think 86, pre 5 speeds were the only ones with them (as a option)... could be wrong.<P>But I have seen more naked fastbacks, or fastbacks with wings, than I have with racks.<P>At least around here.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||06-04-2000||07:44 PM||||Ok, Hoop's right. All the racks I've seen are on notchbacks. Can't say I've ever see one on a fastback except maybe in the pic of Stimpy's car. He did say it was a rare option for GTs, I didn't pick up on that the first time I read it. I'm soooo embarrassed.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||06-04-2000||08:07 PM||||Don't beat yourself up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||bHooper||06-05-2000||06:55 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>jk||||reg||1
Z||000010||Sage||06-05-2000||06:58 AM||||Stimpy:<BR>Batboy pretty much covered the removal process.  Don't remember exact number of fastners.  Only "problem" you may encounter is some of them are cage nuts that you really can't see from underneath.  If the cage starts turning with the bolt, you have to get inventive.  Since I was filling the holes anyway and didn't want to make any new ones underneath, gently, slowly, pried the offender straight up out of the hole and took it apart outside the deck.<P>Note:  Saw a luggage rack the other day that I thought would be a nice touch if you were going to retain it on your car.  It was on a late 80's or early 90's Buick Skylark,(I think!), it was an all chrome rack!  Looked identical to the Fiero's but was all chrome.  Didn't take measurements, but it was exactly the same design.  Just a thought.<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 06-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||stimpy||06-05-2000||07:33 PM||||Pimpin'! Match my 120 spoke Dayton wires!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Seriously, I did check that out myself, but I cant bring myself to chrome anything other then exhaust tips and maybe wheels. Looks like I'm probably just going to get the rear crossbar powdercoated black and mask off the runners well and paint them on the car. Gotta finish my sub enclosure first though.||||reg||1
